                                "sense_id": "8286394f-62c0-34b4-a299-18222e7b89e8",
                                "text": "[page 694:] […] and erugates the belly after birth.\n[page 737:] […] old Hags, to erugate or emend their Faces; herein following the prudence of Galen, though a Pagan, who disallows of not onely the Painting of Faces, but the Tinctures of Hair; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86d8d65e-b128-48fb-816a-a801c57185d3",
                                "sense_id": "8286394f-62c0-34b4-a299-18222e7b89e8",
                                "text": "It purgeth and erugates the face, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "761698ee-67de-41b6-80cc-161415c945cd",
                                "sense_id": "8286394f-62c0-34b4-a299-18222e7b89e8",
                                "text": "Ichthyocolla, (Greek) a kind of glew […] it is […] mixed with glutinative Salves, and others that take away spots and erugate the face."
                            }
                        ]
